{"title":"Radian","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>radian</b> is a unit of measurement for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle\" title=\"Angle\">angles</a>. In a circle, the measure of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Central_angle\" title=\"Central angle\">central angle</a> in radians is the ratio of the length of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intercepted_arc&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Intercepted arc (page does not exist)\">intercepted arc</a> to the length of the circle's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Radius\" title=\"Radius\">radius</a>.\n</p><p>In a unitcircle, a complete angle has measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />, since a complete angle \"intercepts\" the whole circumference of the circle. Thus, radians can be converted to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Degree_(geometry)\" title=\"Degree (geometry)\">degrees</a>: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/8/fa8b020639049f778cff52925b9da264332a29a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi\\; rad=360^\\circ\\implies\\pi \\;rad=180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"262\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Radian&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003329\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 13/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐e